module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Properties.ExtendFiniteType.LocalCohomologyFiniteness
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalCohomology.ComplementSheafCohomology
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalCohomology.HigherDegree.CechModelComparison
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalCohomology.HigherDegree.CechSheafCohomology
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalCohomology.HigherDegree.CechStandardLocalCohomology
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Cohomology.ModuleComparison.HgroupAndCechComplement
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Cohomology.ModuleComparison.SectionsOnOpenDerived

/-!
# `H^p(U, M̃)` is the Čech cohomology of the standard covering, as an `A`-module

Let `A` be a commutative ring, let `I = (f₁, …, f_r)` be an ideal generated by a finite family
and let `U = Spec A \ V(I)`. The cohomology `H^p(U, M̃)` of the sheaf attached to an `A`-module
`M`, read as an `A`-module, is the degree-`p` cohomology of the Čech complex of the covering of
`U` by the basic opens `D(f_i)`, also read as an `A`-module.

This is the **module-valued Čech-to-sheaf comparison**. The abelian-group-valued form is
`Stacks.Cohomology.ModuleComparison.hgroupComplementTildeIsoCechHomology`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.LocalCohomologySequence.complementCohomologyBaseIsoRightDerivedSections` — the two
  spellings of `H^p(U, M̃)` as an `A`-module agree: the one with the scalars restricted in two
  steps, through the global functions, and the one restricting them in a single step.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomologySequence.complementCohomologyBaseIsoDerivedSectionsHomology` —
  `H^p(U, M̃)` is the degree-`p` cohomology of the unbounded derived functor `RΓ(U, -)` that the
  localization triangle of [Stacks, Tag 0DWR] is built from.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomologySequence.complementCohomologyBaseIsoCechHomology` — **`H^p(U, M̃)` is
  the Čech cohomology of the standard covering, as `A`-modules.**

## Main results

* `LocalCohomologySequence.nonempty_complementCohomologyBase_iso_localCohomologyModule_of_cech`
  — granted the one remaining module-valued comparison, [Stacks, Tag 0DWR] (2) holds
  `A`-linearly for a finitely generated ideal of an arbitrary ring.

## Implementation notes

What the comparison does **not** reach is the *algebraic* Čech complex `C^•(f₁, …, f_r; M)` of
[Stacks, Tag 0A6R], whose cohomology is local cohomology. The Čech complex of a covering in the
sense of [Stacks, Tag 01EP], which is what sheaf cohomology is computed by, is the *full* Čech
complex, indexed by all tuples of indices; `C^•(f₁, …, f_r; M)` is the *alternating* one. The
comparison of the two is [Stacks, Tag 01FM], a homotopy equivalence built from the sorting
permutations, and `Stacks.LocalCohomology.cechStandardHomologyIsoCechComplexHomology` reaches it
through `Stacks.Cech.alternatingCechHomologyIso`, whose source and target are
`AddCommGrpCat`-valued complexes. That is why that comparison is an isomorphism of groups and
not of modules, and why the theorem below takes the module-valued form of the step as a
hypothesis instead of proving it.

The hypothesis is stated for an arbitrary finite generating family rather than for a chosen one,
because the conclusion does not mention the family.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DWR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DWR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01EP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01EP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01ET](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01ET)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01FM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01FM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A6R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A6R)
-/


@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.Cohomology.SectionsWithSupport
open Stacks.LocalCohomologyTilde

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard
attribute [local instance] ModuleCat.hasLimitsOfSize
attribute [local instance] AddCommGrpCat.hasLimitsOfSize

universe u

namespace Stacks.LocalCohomologySequence

variable {A : CommRingCat.{u}}

/-! ### The two spellings of `H^p(U, M̃)` over the base ring -/

/-- **The two spellings of `H^p(U, M̃)` as an `A`-module agree.** `H^p(U, M̃)` is reached either by
deriving sections on `U` as modules over the global functions and then reading the result over `A`
— which is `Stacks.LocalCohomologySequence.complementCohomologyBase` — or by deriving
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.sectionsOnAffineComplement`, which restricts the scalars to `A` in one step
before deriving. -/
def complementCohomologyBaseIsoRightDerivedSections (I : Ideal A) (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (p : ℕ) :
    complementCohomologyBase I M p ≅
      ((Stacks.LocalCohomology.sectionsOnAffineComplement A I).rightDerived p).obj
        (Stacks.LocalCohomology.associatedSheaf A M) :=
  (globalToBase A).mapIso
      ((Stacks.Cohomology.ModuleComparison.sectionsOnComplementDerivedIso
          (Spec A).toRingedSpace (zeroLocusSubset I) (isClosed_zeroLocusSubset I) p).app
        (tildeSheaf M)).symm ≪≫
    ((Stacks.LocalCohomology.rightDerivedSectionsOnAffineComplementIso' A I p).app
      (Stacks.LocalCohomology.associatedSheaf A M)).symm

/-- **`H^p(U, M̃)` is the degree-`p` cohomology of `RΓ(U, M̃)`.** The right-hand term of the
affine localization triangle of [Stacks, Tag 0DWR] is the total right derived functor of
sections on `U` on the unbounded derived category; its degree-`p` cohomology at `M̃` placed in
degree zero is the classical `H^p(U, M̃)`, as an `A`-module. -/
def complementCohomologyBaseIsoDerivedSectionsHomology (I : Ideal A) (M : ModuleCat.{u} A)
    (p : ℕ) :
    complementCohomologyBase I M p ≅
      (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) (p : ℤ)).obj
        ((Stacks.LocalCohomology.derivedSectionsOnAffineComplement A I).obj
          ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).Modules 0).obj
            (Stacks.LocalCohomology.associatedSheaf A M))) :=
  complementCohomologyBaseIsoRightDerivedSections I M p ≪≫
    ((Stacks.LocalCohomology.homologyDerivedSectionsNatIsoRightDerived A I p).app
      (Stacks.LocalCohomology.associatedSheaf A M)).symm

/-! ### The module-valued Čech-to-sheaf comparison -/

/-- **`H^p(U, M̃)` is the Čech cohomology of the standard covering, as `A`-modules.** Let `I` be
generated by the finite family `f` and let `U = Spec A \ V(I)`, covered by the basic opens
`D(f_i)`. For every `p` the `A`-module `H^p(U, M̃)` is the degree-`p` cohomology of the Čech
complex of [Stacks, Tag 01EP] of that covering with coefficients in `M̃`, with its scalars
restricted from `Γ(U, 𝒪)` to `A`.

This is the module-valued form of
`Stacks.Cohomology.ModuleComparison.hgroupComplementTildeIsoCechHomology`. No hypothesis on `A` and
none on `I` beyond the existence of the generating family `f` is used. -/
def complementCohomologyBaseIsoCechHomology (I : Ideal A) {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A)
    (hIf : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = I) (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (p : ℕ) :
    complementCohomologyBase I M p ≅
      (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u, u, u}
          (Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementOpenScalars I)).obj
        ((Stacks.Cohomology.CechSheaf.cechComplex.{u, u, u, u}
            (Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementZeroLocus A I)
            (Stacks.LocalCohomology.cechStandardOpen f)
            (Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen f I hIf)
            (Stacks.LocalCohomology.associatedSheaf A M)).homology p) :=
  complementCohomologyBaseIsoDerivedSectionsHomology I M p ≪≫
    Stacks.LocalCohomology.homologyDerivedSectionsIsoCechCohomology f I hIf M p ≪≫
    (ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u, u, u}
        (Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementOpenScalars I)).mapIso
      (Stacks.LocalCohomology.cechPlusHomologyIso
        (Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementZeroLocus A I)
        (Stacks.LocalCohomology.cechStandardOpen f)
        (Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen f I hIf)
        (Stacks.LocalCohomology.associatedSheaf A M) p)

/-! ### What closing [Stacks, Tag 0DWR] (2) `A`-linearly still needs -/

/-- **The remaining comparison holds after forgetting the `A`-module structure.** For `p = q + 1`
above zero, the Čech complex of the standard covering read over `A` and the extended alternating
Čech complex of `f` have the same cohomology *as abelian groups*, in degrees `p` and `p + 1`. -/
theorem nonempty_forget₂_cechHomology_iso_extendedCechHomology (I : Ideal A) {r : ℕ}
    (f : Fin r → A) (hIf : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = I) (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (q : ℕ) :
    Nonempty ((forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj
        ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u, u, u}
            (Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementOpenScalars I)).obj
          ((Stacks.Cohomology.CechSheaf.cechComplex.{u, u, u, u}
              (Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementZeroLocus A I)
              (Stacks.LocalCohomology.cechStandardOpen f)
              (Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen f I hIf)
              (Stacks.LocalCohomology.associatedSheaf A M)).homology (q + 1))) ≅
      (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).obj
        ((Stacks.LocalCohomology.extendedCechComplex f M).homology
          (((q + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) + 1))) := by
  have hdeg : (((q + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) + 1) = (q : ℤ) + 2 := by push_cast; ring
  rw [hdeg]
  exact ⟨Stacks.Cohomology.ModuleComparison.cechComplexHomologyForgetIso
      (Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementZeroLocus A I)
      (Stacks.LocalCohomology.cechStandardOpen f)
      (Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen f I hIf)
      (Stacks.LocalCohomology.associatedSheaf A M) (q + 1) ≪≫
    Stacks.LocalCohomology.cechStandardHomologyIsoCechComplexHomology f M q ≪≫
    (forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} A) AddCommGrpCat.{u}).mapIso
      (Stacks.LocalCohomology.extendedCechHomologyIso f M q).symm⟩

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0DWR] (2) `A`-linearly for a finitely generated ideal, granted the
module-valued form of [Stacks, Tag 01FM].** Let `I` be a finitely generated ideal of a
commutative ring `A`, let `U = Spec A \ V(I)` and let `M` be an `A`-module. If, for every finite
generating family of `I`, the Čech complex of the standard covering read over `A` has the
cohomology of the extended alternating Čech complex of that family one degree up, then the
`A`-module `H^p(U, M̃)` is the local cohomology `H^{p+1}_{V(I)}(M)`. -/
theorem nonempty_complementCohomologyBase_iso_localCohomologyModule_of_cech
    (I : Ideal A) (hI : I.FG) (M : ModuleCat.{u} A) (p : ℕ)
    (h : ∀ {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A) (hIf : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = I),
      Nonempty ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars.{u, u, u}
            (Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementOpenScalars I)).obj
          ((Stacks.Cohomology.CechSheaf.cechComplex.{u, u, u, u}
              (Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementZeroLocus A I)
              (Stacks.LocalCohomology.cechStandardOpen f)
              (Stacks.LocalCohomology.complementZeroLocus_eq_iSup_cechStandardOpen f I hIf)
              (Stacks.LocalCohomology.associatedSheaf A M)).homology p) ≅
        (Stacks.LocalCohomology.extendedCechComplex f M).homology ((p : ℤ) + 1))) :
    Nonempty (complementCohomologyBase I M p ≅
      Stacks.LocalCohomology.localCohomologyModule A I hI M ((p : ℤ) + 1)) := by
  obtain ⟨r, f, hIf⟩ := Submodule.fg_iff_exists_fin_generating_family.1 hI
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := h f hIf
  exact ⟨complementCohomologyBaseIsoCechHomology I f hIf M p ≪≫ e ≪≫
    (Stacks.LocalCohomology.localCohomologyIsoExtendedCechHomology f M I hI hIf
      ((p : ℤ) + 1)).symm⟩

end Stacks.LocalCohomologySequence

end
